<description>CERNQ52 Ver004: ground positions from which the whole of the luminous trajectory (95% EARLIEST, MEDIAN (weighted mean) and 95% LATEST arrival; 90 km to 20 km) can be seen: observer at sea level on the WGS84 ellipsoid, standard refraction, no terrain. Green outline: whole trajectory visible, about 692,800 km^2. Yellow outline: the tops (90 km points) visible, about 3,087,676 km^2. The e-mail is confidential and the object unconfirmed: do not distribute.</description>
